    "blurb": "The show delivers a blistering Playin' in the Band, a razor‑sharp Truckin' > Drums > The Other One sequence, and a rousing Promised Land finale. Jerry’s leads are focused throughout while Phil provides powerful bass bursts. Soundboard sources capture the high‑energy performance with excellent clarity.",
    "review": "May 16, 1972 at Studio du Grand Theatre finds the Dead locked in a tight, high‑octane groove that epitomizes Europe ’72. The first set builds momentum with a soaring Playin' in the Band and a crisp, bluesy It Hurts Me Too from Pigpen, while Jerry’s wah‑wah licks on Playin' and his searing leads through China Cat > Rider keep the energy cooking. The second set explodes into a legendary Truckin' > Drums > The Other One stretch—Jerry’s laser‑focused soloing rides Phil’s thunderous bass, and Bill Kreutzmann drives the jam with crisp, propulsive beats. The band wraps up with a punchy Promised Land that leaves the crowd buzzing, making this night one of the standout snapshots of the 1972 European tour.",
